{# goal: Rendering template — surfaces the quadrant chart (from map-value-chain) and strategic recommendations (from synthesize-recommendations) as a single markdown string containing a fenced ```mermaid block. This is the process's final user-facing output: without it, the diagram stays buried in an intermediate step result and never reaches the chat stream. Deterministic (no LLM call). #}
{# Surface the Wardley Map quadrant chart + recommendations as markdown.
   This is a pure Jinja2 template (the [inference] header carries only the render contract; no LLM call) rendered by
   the `render_template` tool from the SKILL.md body's final step.

   The fenced ```mermaid block is what acp_thread's mermaid renderer picks up —
   parse_mermaid_info requires the info string "mermaid" on a fenced code block,
   and is_supported_diagram_type checks that the first token is quadrantChart.
   Without this render step, map_diagram stays buried inside the map-value-chain
   step's JSON output and the final surfaced text has no diagram. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    map_diagram:
      type: string
      non_blank: true
    recommendations: array
    rationale:
      type: string
      required: false
  output:
    markdown: string
---
## Wardley Map

```mermaid
{{ map_diagram }}
```

## Strategic Recommendations

{% for rec in recommendations %}
- **{{ rec.category | default("N/A") }}** — {{ rec.component | default("N/A") }}: {{ rec.recommendation | default("") }} (priority: {{ rec.priority | default("N/A") }}, confidence: {{ rec.confidence | default("N/A") }})
  - {{ rec.rationale | default("") }}
{% endfor %}

## Assessment

{{ rationale | default("No rationale provided.") }}
